  "query_preview": "/WEDNESDAY THROUGH TUESDAY/...\nIssued at 158 PM MDT Tue Aug 4 2026\n\nOver the long term our CWA heats back up to the mid 90s to low 100s, \nbringing back our seasonal warm temperatures. As the ridge builds, \nwarm dry air comes into the area, which will bring a risk of \ncritical fire weather conditions throughout the week. Temperatures \nbegin to heat up Thursday and into the weekend bringing those mid \n90s to low 100s across the CWA. 700mb temperatures show values in \nthe mid teens, supporting seasonal temperatures. Over the weekend, \nthe ridge begins to flatten out, tightening the pressure gradient \nover the northern areas of the CWA, bringing stronger winds and slim \nchances of precipitation. Elevated fire weather conditions continue \nover through the weekend with the warm dry air, little to no \nprecipitation, and marginally breezy winds.",
